2	 * local-docker profile factory.
3	 *
4	 * Bundles the Wave-4 adapter set into a RuntimePorts instance for the
5	 * M:N multi-container topology: each orchestrator spawns per-task executor
6	 * containers via `docker run -d`; all completions route through a shared
7	 * Redis-backed broker service.
8	 *
9	 * Adapter set:
10	 *   ExecutorPort         → DockerRunAdapter     (docker run -d, --network agents-net)
11	 *   CompletionBrokerPort → HttpBrokerAdapter    (calls Go broker service at BROKER_URL)
12	 *   BriefingTransport    → LocalFileBriefingAdapter
13	 *   WorkflowState        → GitWorkflowStateAdapter
14	 *   Credential           → EnvCredentialAdapter
15	 *   WorkspacePull        → GitClonePullAdapter
16	 *   EventEmitter         → StdoutJsonEmitter
17	 *   Scheduler            → SimpleSleepScheduler
18	 *   Clock                → RealClock
19	 *
20	 * Topology:
21	 *   - All orchestrator containers, executor containers, the broker container,
22	 *     and the Redis container share the `agents-net` bridge network.
23	 *   - Orchestrators have the Docker socket mounted so they can `docker run`
24	 *     executor containers attached to the same bridge.
25	 *   - Runners reach the broker at http://broker:7000/callback via service-name DNS.
26	 *   - Any orchestrator drains any completion (opportunistic dispatch).
27	 */
